# Abyssal Harvester: "{T}: Exile target creature card from a graveyard that was put there this turn. Create a token that's a copy of it,
# except it's a Nightmare in addition to its other types. Then exile all other Nightmare tokens you control." Both players cast one
# on turn 1 and 2. Turn 3: Bot1 kills its Walking Corpse with a Lightning Bolt and does not use its Harvester. Turn 4: Bot2 does the same
# and makes a Nightmare token with its Harvester, a copy of its own Corpse (the Harvester tapped, its cost paid). Turn 5: Bot1's turn-3 Corpse
# was put into its graveyard on an earlier turn, so it is refused as a target, the Bolt (a noncreature card put there this turn) too; a
# Corpse killed this turn is taken and copied, exiled (not in the graveyard), and the token is a Nightmare Zombie that stays. Turn 7: Bot1
# kills Bot2's Harvester with a Bolt and takes it from the opponent's graveyard (a creature card from any graveyard): the token is a copy of
# it, with its ability, a Nightmare in addition, and Bot1's turn-5 Nightmare token is exiled while Bot2's own Nightmare token stays,
# and the new one is not exiled.

